CPebble
	CPebble is an experiment at a modern and de-cluttered re-write of
    	Pebble in C. At some point this will be re-named to Pebble once
    	it is deemed stable enough to replace the current Zig version.
	The older Zig version can be viewed at ../../old/ relative to
	this current path.
	Please note this does not fully implement pebble schematics
	yet and is a work-in-progress, unlike the Zig version, which
	is feature-complete.
    	As the Zig version, the license can be viewed at
	http://thenuoviorizzonticompany.org/license/openlicense/3.txt

Building from source
	Building from source requires only a C99 libc, a C99 compiler,
	and a POSIX make build system. Various variables can be used during
	building, such as

	target - target operating system to build for - view the platform support
		list to know what to place here. The default is 'c', which uses
		pure C99 + Libc.

	graphics - graphics library to use. The default is none.

	build - the type of build to use - these include fast, debug, and
		default. The default is 'default'. Please note fast builds
		are not guaranteed to work on any machine besides the host
		compiling.

	analyzer - the name of the static analyzer to use when building.
		No default, not required.

	cc - the selected C compiler to use - defaults to 'cc'.

	program - the path to place the finished binary - defaults to
		'./bin/vm'.

	cflags - the C compiler flags to use before adding the build-specific
		compiler flags. The default is '-std=c99'.

	By default, CPebble builds as a static binary, meaning it requires
	no runtime dependencies.

	If you do not have a POSIX make system, one was provided under the
	bootstrap/ directory. The software from said directory was not written
	by us, but instead by Ron Yorston as part of the pdpmake project. 

	To bootstrap the build system, run the command

	$ cc -o make bootstrap/*.c
	
	from the current directory. 

	The readme file in the bootstrap/ directory may provide more information
	on this software.

	Software provided in this directory has been re-licensed under the same 
	license as this project, as it was previously released to the public 
	domain. All pieces of code that could not be re-licensed have been 
	removed from the tree in this copy. 

	Give a big thanks to him, he does some great work. Check him out at
	https://github.com/rmyorston

Supported Platforms
	All supported platforms include:

		freestand 	-> freestanding
					The common denominator

		c 		-> pure C99 & Libc + platform freestand
					Differences between freestand:
					  - Adds extra libraries for core VM 
					    functionality which use a C99 Libc

		unix		-> UNIX kernel and POSIX Libc + platform c
					Differences between c:
					  - Adds kernel-backed random number generation
					    based on /dev/urandom instead of the software
					    C algorithm using nondeterministic hardware
					    behavior

		openbsd 	-> OpenBSD kernel and Libc + platform unix
					Differences between unix:
					  - Adds OpenBSD pledge(2) and unveil(2) system
					    calls to initialization code
					  - Uses OpenBSD arc4random(3) instead of the UNIX
					    /dev/urandom

		puredarwin	-> Darwin/PureDarwin kernel and Libc + platform unix
					Differences between unix:
					  - Adds PureDarwin-specific Libc shims

	Depreciated platforms include:

		puredarwin
			Random number generation is currently not provided.

	For a list of tested environments, please visit 
		- http://pebblevm.org/platforms.html	

